Z||000007||StuGood||11-23-2000||04:05 AM||||hugh, do I understand you to say that cranes are more expensive than tow trucks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">? <P>Well, I'm glad no one got hurt.  Reminds me of the time I left my 1986 SE in gear (motor off) in my short driveway.  Just long enough to shut the garage door, you know.  I looked up, and the thing had slipped out of gear, it was rolling backwards down the driveway into the street!  Couldn't believe how quickly it picked up speed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">. It rolled across the street and <B>smacked</B> into the curb.<P>Fortunately, no other cars (or kids  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">!) happened by at the time.  The height of the curb was such that it squarely hit the back of the frame (cradle?) below the fascia - <B>no</B> damage to the body!  Just applied paint to the scraped areas of the frame to prevent rust, and it was good as new  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !   <P>Thank God for cheap lessons  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !  Now I always apply the brake and turn the wheel, even if I leave the car just for a sec.  ||||reg||12
Z||000008||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||08:24 AM||||With any luck, a hard rain will come and wash that Ford away!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
